          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            typically imply – or are even equivalent to (
            %a{:href => "#CandielloLechner93"}> Candiello-Lechner 93
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Howe97"} Howe 97
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertorsion"} super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+Cartan+connection"} torsion
            of the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein+fields"} vielbein fields
            vanishes. At least in some cases these
            %em supergravity torsion constraints
            may naturally be understood as saying that supergravity solutions are (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"}> higher
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartan+geometry"} super-Cartan geometry
            modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetime"} extended super Minkowski spacetime
            %em with
            its canonical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+G-structure"} torsion of a G-structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+invariant+1-forms"} left invariant 1-forms
            on super-Minkowski space are not closed.
          %h3#CanonicalTorsionOfSuperMinkowskiSpacetime From the canonical torsion of super-Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            The torsion constraint is naturally understood by regarding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            for the inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+group"} super Poincare group
            and by noticing that the corresponding local model space, which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d|N}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi θ
                    %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x^a, \theta^\alpha)
            be the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinates"} coordinates
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d|N}
            underlying the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+group"} super translation group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left-invariant+1-forms"} left-invariant 1-forms
            are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi α
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi^\alpha = d \theta^\alpha
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mover
                        %mi θ
                        %mo ¯
                      %msup
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi a
                      %mi d
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^a = d x^a + \frac{i}{2} \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a d \theta
                \.
          %p
            Here the extra summand in the equation for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^a
            (necessary to make it left-invariant) causes it to be non-closed:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi x
                            %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mfrac
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mi d
                          %mi θ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mi d
                          %mover
                            %mi θ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mi d
                          %mi θ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mi ψ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  d e^a &amp; = d (d x^a + \frac{i}{2} \overline{\theta} \Gamma^a d \theta)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} d \overline{\theta}\Gamma^a d \theta
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} \overline{\psi}\Gamma^a \psi
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\omega^a{}_b)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d|N}
            to vanish, as usual, this means that there is non-vanishing
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi τ
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %msup
                            %mi ω
                            %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mi b
                          %mo ∧
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi e
                            %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mover
                            %mi ψ
                            %mo ¯
                          %msup
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi a
                          %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\tau^a &amp; = \mathbf{d} e^a + \omega^a{}_b \wedge e^b
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \mathbf{d} e^a
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \frac{i}{2} \overline{\psi}\Gamma^a \psi
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            Depending on perspective one might say that it is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supertorsion"} supertorsion
            that vanishes (see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
            and at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
            for this perspective), or, alternatively, that one is dealing with
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            whose local model space carries non-vanishing torsion, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#InTermsOfTorsionTwistedGStructure"} below
          %p
            Notice that the torison-full but left-invariant forms are of course obtained from the torsion-free but non-left-invartiant forms by a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathbb{R}^{d|N})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi e
                              %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi ψ
                              %mi α
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                              %mfrac
                                %mi i
                                %mn 2
                            %msup
                              %mi Γ
                              %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi α
                                %mi β
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mi α
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
