            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            This perspective on the torsion constraints in supergravity is adopted in (
            %a{:href => "#Lott01"}> Lott 01
            ), see there around (38) of the original article or section 4 of the review on the arXiv.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_supergravity_equations_of_motion Relation to supergravity equations of motion
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            typically imply the torsion constraints. See at
            %a{:href => "Green-Schwarz+action+functional#OnCurvedSpacetime"} super p-brane – On curved spacetimes
            for more.
          %p
            With enough
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bianchi+identities"} Bianchi identities
            on the superfields, see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fre+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fre formulation of supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (
            %a{:href => "#CandielloLechner93"}> Candiello-Lechner 93
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Howe97"} Howe 97
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CederwallGranNilssonTsimpis04"} Cederwall-Gran-Nilsson-Tsimpis 04, section 2.4
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactifications"} KK-compactifications
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#Examples11dSuGra"} Examples – 11d SuGra
          %h3#relation_to_crgeometry Relation to CR-geometry
          %p
            A close
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analogy
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CR+geometry"} CR geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetimes"} superspacetimes
            (as both being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+of+a+G-structure"} torsion-ful
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+G-structures"} integrable G-structures
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lott01"} Lott 01 exposition (4.2)
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            In accord with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#CanonicalTorsionOfSuperMinkowskiSpacetime"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theory constrain the spinorial part of the torsion to have components
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
